  "decision": "Preserve as an experimental branch. On the three-floor hold the selective direct path saves 0.11 s while leaving a 0.46 s gap to the matched Manyan median. On six floors it saves 2.49 s (3.7%) with 17,512 KiB additional peak RSS in one matched pair. Revisit when compact original-edge storage or a shared labeling loop can avoid a second full-column classifier and contain mixed-row fallback cost.",
  "limitations": [
    "One six-floor pair. Four-floor peak RSS varied across processes. No inference across hosts, semaphore counts or search schedules.",
    "Eligible direct columns are based on the actual scanned store-owned original rows and the complete original Boolean guards. Nonmatching actions, incomparable values, unknown labels or a late wide row can require fallback for the whole attempted column. Additional engineering would need a single row-level classifier or bounded progressive fallback and explicit inactive-action demand.",
    "The prototype increments producer_images on a successful-column source with a matching emission, even when no original demanded term reads it. Use the explicit direct_image counters to compare this implementation; do not infer savings from producer_images alone."
  ]
}
